# netsurf: a batch whose only obstacle is a stylesheet still loading waits for it (patch 442)
# Generated 2026-11-22
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 441)
#
# "a sheet is still loading or changing" (sheet change and sheet removal,
# ~6 a load on 7 sites: google, bbc, oldreddit) sent the batch to the full
# rebuild: 415's whole-document re-cascade cannot be made from a sheet in
# flight (html_css_new_selection_context asserts on one). That sheet marks
# again when it is done (html_css_mark_sheets counts it into the same
# window, 436), and the re-cascade then sees every sheet.
#
# When the batch declined only for that reason -- before anything in it
# was answered (a batch of sheet marks alone, or its first mark), or after
# its precise marks were answered (they stand; the slot drops them and
# keeps only its sheet marks) -- macos9_reconvert_cb keeps the slot and
# retries it every RECONVERT_SHEET_RETRY_MS (100) for at most
# RECONVERT_SHEET_WAIT_MAX_MS (1500), then takes the full rebuild as
# before. Later marks join the waiting slot. html_rl_doc_noop flags the
# reason (html_rl_take_unsettled) and, while the batch may still wait
# (html_rl_sheet_wait_ok), logs "waits (...)" instead of "declined (...)",
# so the census counts only real declines. A synchronous flush (a script's
# layout read) cannot wait and is unchanged.
#
